docs {
  # Environment Management Tests
  
  Tests for environment registration and management APIs.
  
  ## What Are Environments?
  
  Environments represent applications (Consumers, Providers, or Brokers) that interact with the SIF Unity Broker. Each environment has:
  - Unique session token for authentication
  - Shared secret for HMAC signature generation
  - Application metadata (name, type, instance ID)
  - Associated ACL entries for permissions
  
  ## Tests Included
  
  - Create environment (success and validation errors)
  - List environments
  - Get environment by ID
  - Update environment
  - Delete environment
  - Error scenarios (404, 400)
  
  ## Important Notes
  
  - POST /environments does NOT require authentication (bootstrap endpoint)
  - All other environment operations require authentication
  - Deleting an environment revokes its session token
  - Test environments are prefixed with `bruno-test`
}
